    <statement><p>Let <m>\&gt;l\&gt;</m> be the length of a diagonal of a rectangle whose sides have lengths <m>\&gt;x\&gt;</m> and <m>\&gt;y\&gt;</m>, and assume that <m>\&gt;x\&gt;</m> and <m>\&gt;y\&gt;</m> vary with time.</p>
<p>If <m>\&gt;x\&gt;</m> increases at a constant rate of <m>\&gt; \frac {1} {7}\&gt;</m> ft/s and <m>\&gt;y\&gt;</m> decreases at a constant rate of <m>\&gt; \frac {1} {8}\&gt;</m> ft/s, how fast is the size of the diagonal changing when <m>\&gt;x = 3\&gt;</m> ft. and <m>\&gt;y = 4\&gt;</m> ft?</p>
<p>Answer: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-0.0142857142857143</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
